&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To answer this question, let&amp;#39;s first understand the meaning of the word given in the question:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Remedy:&lt;/strong&gt; a medicine or treatment for a disease or injury; a means of counteracting or eliminating something undesirable; a legal means to recover a right or to prevent or obtain redress for a wrong. (&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;उपाय, चिकित्सा, निवारण&lt;/span&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Now, let&amp;#39;s examine the given sentences:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sentence A:&lt;/strong&gt; The herbal remedy she used alleviated her cold symptoms significantly.
	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;This sentence &lt;strong&gt;correctly&lt;/strong&gt; uses the word &amp;quot;&lt;strong&gt;remedy&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;quot; in the context of a treatment for cold symptoms.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sentence B:&lt;/strong&gt; He looked for a remedy to fix the broken clock but couldn&amp;#39;t find one.
	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;This sentence &lt;strong&gt;does not correctly&lt;/strong&gt; use the word &amp;quot;remedy&amp;quot; because &amp;quot;remedy&amp;quot; is typically used for treatments related to health or legal solutions, not for fixing mechanical items.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sentence C:&lt;/strong&gt; The court provided a legal remedy for the plaintiff in the dispute.
	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;This sentence &lt;strong&gt;correctly&lt;/strong&gt; uses the word &amp;quot;&lt;strong&gt;remedy&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;quot; in the context of a legal solution provided by the court.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;u&gt;So, &lt;strong&gt;only sentences A and C correctly use&lt;/strong&gt; the word &amp;quot;remedy&amp;quot; to illustrate different contexts of treatments or legal solutions.&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Therefore, the correct answer is&lt;strong&gt; &amp;quot;Both A &amp;amp; C.&amp;quot;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div&gt;Let the radius of circle A = 3x&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;And the radius of circle B = 2x&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;22/7*(3x)2 &amp;ndash; 22/7*(2x)2 = 770&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;9x&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;ndash; 4x&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;&amp;nbsp;= 770*7/22&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;5x&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;&amp;nbsp;= 245&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;x&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;= 49&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;x = 7&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;The radius of circle B = 2*7 = 14 cm&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;The perimeter of circle B= 2*22/7*14 = 88 cm&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;Option&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;A is right.&lt;/div&gt;

