&lt;p&gt;Here are the other options explained along with their Hindi meanings and why they are incorrect:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 1 (A-B)&lt;/strong&gt;: &amp;quot;Surge crash&amp;quot; (अचानक ध्वस्त) is illogical and does not fit the sentence structure.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 2 (C-D)&lt;/strong&gt;: &amp;quot;Frustrated accounts&amp;quot; (हताश खाते) is nonsensical and grammatically wrong.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 3 (B-C)&lt;/strong&gt;: &amp;quot;Crash frustrated&amp;quot; (ध्वस्त हताश) is meaningless in this context.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 4 (A-D)&lt;/strong&gt;: &amp;quot;Surge accounts&amp;quot; (अचानक खाते) is illogical and does not convey proper meaning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The correct answer is: &lt;b&gt;Option 2) B-D&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The word &lt;strong&gt;&amp;quot;Overlooked&amp;quot;&lt;/strong&gt; means ignored, neglected, or not given proper attention. (नज़रअंदाज़ करना)

	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Example:&lt;/strong&gt; Important cultural traditions were overlooked in the modern curriculum.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;quot;Celebrate&amp;quot;&lt;/strong&gt; means to honor, praise, or recognize something with respect or festivities. (जश्न मनाना/सम्मान करना)
	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Example:&lt;/strong&gt; The festival celebrates the rich heritage of the community.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Correct usage: &amp;quot;highlight the cultural heritage, celebrate their traditional practices, and preserve the historical narratives often overlooked by mainstream media&amp;quot; makes the sentence grammatically correct and meaningful.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Therefore, the correct answer is: &lt;strong&gt;Option 2) B-D&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Additional Information&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here are the other options explained along with their Hindi meanings and why they are incorrect:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 1 (A-C)&lt;/strong&gt;: &amp;quot;Highlight preserve&amp;quot; (उजागर करना संरक्षित करना) is redundant and does not correct the grammatical error.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 3 (A-B and C-D)&lt;/strong&gt;: Interchanging both pairs distorts meaning; &amp;quot;highlight overlooked&amp;quot; (उजागर करना नज़रअंदाज़ करना) is contradictory.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 4 (C-D)&lt;/strong&gt;: &amp;quot;Preserve celebrate&amp;quot; (संरक्षित करना जश्न मनाना) is grammatically awkward and illogical in this context.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 5 (No interchange required)&lt;/strong&gt;: Without interchange, the sentence remains incorrect because &amp;quot;preserve the historical narratives often celebrate&amp;quot; is ungrammatical.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The correct answer is: &lt;b&gt;Option 1) A-D&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The word &lt;strong&gt;&amp;quot;Rates&amp;quot;&lt;/strong&gt; refers to measurable quantities such as interest rates, growth rates, or inflation rates. (दरें)

	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Example:&lt;/strong&gt; Inflation rates have been rising steadily over the past year.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;quot;Stability&amp;quot;&lt;/strong&gt; means a state of being steady, balanced, and not prone to sudden changes. (स्थिरता)
	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Example:&lt;/strong&gt; Economic stability is crucial for long-term development.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Correct usage: &amp;quot;Economic stability is generally achieved when a country manages to control its national debt, reduce consumer prices, and maintain low unemployment rates.&amp;quot; (आर्थिक स्थिरता सामान्यतः तब प्राप्त होती है जब देश अपने राष्ट्रीय ऋण को नियंत्रित करता है, उपभोक्ता कीमतों को कम करता है और कम बेरोजगारी दर बनाए रखता है)।&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Therefore, the correct answer is: &lt;strong&gt;Option 1) A-D&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Additional Information&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here are the other options explained along with their Hindi meanings and why they are incorrect:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 2 (B-C)&lt;/strong&gt;: &amp;quot;Control reduce&amp;quot; (नियंत्रण कम करना) is redundant and does not fix the grammatical error.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 3 (A-B)&lt;/strong&gt;: &amp;quot;Rates control&amp;quot; (दरें नियंत्रण) is awkward and does not make sense in this context.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 4 (C-D)&lt;/strong&gt;: &amp;quot;Reduce stability&amp;quot; (स्थिरता कम करना) is illogical; stability should be maintained, not reduced.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 5 (No interchange required)&lt;/strong&gt;: Without interchange, the sentence remains incorrect because &amp;quot;economic rates&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;unemployment stability&amp;quot; are ungrammatical and illogical.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The correct answer is: &lt;b&gt;Option 2) A-C&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The word &lt;strong&gt;&amp;quot;Exacerbate&amp;quot;&lt;/strong&gt; means to make a problem, situation, or negative condition worse. (बदतर करना)

	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Example:&lt;/strong&gt; Cutting down forests will only exacerbate the effects of climate change.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;quot;Ameliorate&amp;quot;&lt;/strong&gt; means to improve or make a bad situation better. (सुधारना)
	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Example:&lt;/strong&gt; New policies were introduced to ameliorate the living conditions of the poor.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Correct usage: &amp;quot;ameliorate the deleterious effects of the crisis&amp;quot; (संकट के हानिकारक प्रभावों को सुधारना) and &amp;quot;exacerbate the situation into something less salubrious&amp;quot; (स्थिति को और कम स्वास्थ्यकर बनाना) make the sentence grammatically correct and meaningful.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Therefore, the correct answer is: &lt;strong&gt;Option 2) A-C&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Additional Information&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here are the other options explained along with their Hindi meanings and why they are incorrect:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 1 (B-D)&lt;/strong&gt;: &amp;quot;Deleterious salubrious&amp;quot; (हानिकारक स्वास्थ्यकर) are antonyms; interchanging them distorts meaning.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 3 (A-B and C-D)&lt;/strong&gt;: Swapping both pairs makes the sentence contradictory and illogical.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 4 (C-D)&lt;/strong&gt;: &amp;quot;Ameliorate salubrious&amp;quot; (स्वास्थ्यकर सुधारना) is awkward and does not fit the context.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 5 (No interchange required)&lt;/strong&gt;: Without interchange, the sentence is incorrect because &amp;quot;exacerbate the deleterious effects&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;ameliorate into something less salubrious&amp;quot; are contradictory and ungrammatical.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The correct answer is: &lt;b&gt;Option 3) A-C&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The word &lt;strong&gt;&amp;quot;Obsequious&amp;quot;&lt;/strong&gt; means excessively obedient or servile, often to gain favor. (चापलूस)

	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Example:&lt;/strong&gt; The obsequious assistant agreed with everything the boss said.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;quot;Recalcitrant&amp;quot;&lt;/strong&gt; means stubbornly resistant to authority or control; uncooperative. (हठी/अनुशासनहीन)
	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Example:&lt;/strong&gt; The recalcitrant worker refused to follow company rules.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Correct usage: &amp;quot;The recalcitrant employee refused to follow orders, displaying an intransigent attitude that contrasted sharply with the obsequious behavior of his sycophantic peers.&amp;quot; This makes the sentence grammatically correct and meaningful.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Therefore, the correct answer is: &lt;strong&gt;Option 3) A-C&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Additional Information&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here are the other options explained along with their Hindi meanings and why they are incorrect:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 1 (A-D)&lt;/strong&gt;: &amp;quot;Obsequious sycophantic&amp;quot; (चापलूस चापलूस) are synonyms; interchanging them does not fix the logical error.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 2 (B-C)&lt;/strong&gt;: &amp;quot;Intransigent recalcitrant&amp;quot; (अड़ियल हठी) are near synonyms; swapping them does not improve sentence logic.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 4 (B-D)&lt;/strong&gt;: &amp;quot;Intransigent sycophantic&amp;quot; (अड़ियल चापलूस) is contradictory and illogical in this context.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 5 (No interchange required)&lt;/strong&gt;: Without interchange, the sentence remains incorrect because &amp;quot;obsequious employee refused to follow orders&amp;quot; is contradictory; an obsequious person would obey, not refuse.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
